{"name":"Belfast","hex":"#558d4f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Belfast","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The capital and largest city of Northern Ireland.","A place named for either the city in Northern Ireland or another place also named as such.\nA suburb of Christchurch, Canterbury, New Zealand. \nA town in Mpumalanga, South Africa.\nA community and rural municipality in Queens County, Prince Edward Island, Canada.\nA locale in the United States:\nAn unincorporated community in Lassen County, California; named for the city in Maine.\nAn unincorporated community in Bryan County, Georgia.\nA city, the county seat of Waldo County, Maine. \nA township in Murray County, Minnesota.\nAn unincorporated community in Newton County, Missouri.\nA ghost town in Greeley County, Nebraska.\nA town and census-designated place therein, in Allegany County, New York. \nAn unincorporated community in Clermont County, Ohio.\nAn unincorporated community in Highland County, Ohio.\nA ghost town in Licking County, Ohio.\nA township in Fulton County, Pennsylvania.\nA census-designated place in Plainfield Township, Northampton County, Pennsylvania.\nAn unincorporated community in Marshall County, Tennessee."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Belfast"}],"entries":[{"title":"Belfast","blocks":[{"text":"Belfast is the capital, largest city and main port of Northern Ireland. It stands on the banks of the river Lagan, and is connected to the open sea through Belfast Lough and the North Channel. The city is the most populous in Northern Ireland and the second-largest, after Dublin, on the island of Ireland, with a recorded population in 2021 of 345,418 and of 704,406 for the greater metropolitan area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Belfast_Skyline_City_Quays.png/330px-Belfast_Skyline_City_Quays.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org